<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">California Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1846 CE – 1846 CE · capital Sonoma</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Bear Flag Republic, a 25-day revolt by American settlers in Mexican California whose flag became the state flag of California.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In June 1846, as war between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> began, American settlers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacramento-valley">Sacramento Valley</a> feared expulsion by Mexican authorities in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alta-california">Alta California</a>. Encouraged by the explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-c-fremont">John C. Frémont</a>, about 30 of them seized the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonoma-california">Sonoma</a> on 14 June and took the local commander, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-guadalupe-vallejo">Mariano Guadalupe Vallejo</a>, prisoner.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The rebels proclaimed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> Republic, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-b-ide">William B. Ide</a> as their leader, and raised a flag with a grizzly bear, a star and the words 'California Republic', painted by William Todd. The republic had no real institutions and controlled little beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonoma-california">Sonoma</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacramento-valley">Sacramento Valley</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-c-fremont">Frémont</a> took command of its forces, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california-battalion">California Battalion</a>, in early July.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 7 July 1846 Commodore <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-d-sloat">John Sloat</a> raised the American flag at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monterey-california">Monterey</a>, and the Stars and Stripes replaced the Bear Flag at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonoma-california">Sonoma</a> on 9 July. The republic dissolved into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/occupation-of-japan">American occupation</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> became a state in 1850, adopting a version of the bear flag in 1911.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/california-republic.jpg" alt="California Republic" width="320" height="208"><figcaption>Image: Smurrayinchester · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_Bear_Flag_of_California_(1846).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1846 CE – 1846 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sonoma</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William B. Ide</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bear Flag Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=california-republic" aria-label="California Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1634 802 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where California Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M1954 1058L1937 1114M1954 1058L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M1937 1114h0M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M1954 1058h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M1954 1058h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sonoma. <a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=california-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
